scope_limits:
APPROVED (scoped), with no Critical, High or Medium findings:
- the curated composition SOURCE of attempt.rs, custody.rs, custody_tests.rs, mod.rs and session.rs onto main 768f843, as a private, cfg(test)-activated mechanical preparation-custody component;
- the selected design and evidence documents, README and master text, as truthful within their stated limits, subject to the Finding 4 wording.

Regression attribution: no code path from the selected changes reaches the failing Grok consumers.
- Grok is untouched.
- custody_pool is None outside cfg(test).
- file_factory is None in all pre-existing tests, and the legacy Codex paths are equivalent to main.
The only conceivable channel is shared-process load from the 18 added controls:
- 21 or more concurrent custodian threads, each polling at 1 ms;
- worker threads;
- about twenty temporary Git repositories;
- two ApprovalFixture setups running bounded_git under process-group inspection alongside the other suites.
That channel is unmeasured. The packet's passing and failing runs with the mechanics present come from different trees and hosts. Cause and component contribution remain UNKNOWN, and nothing here explains or discharges the RED results.

Not exercised or approved:
- the Ok/Starting post-return endpoint;
- custody on the supervise(), finish_preparation_error, CheckpointCommitted or terminal paths (finish_preparation_error calls finished() directly and would retain an outstanding resource without a deferred disposition);
- the long-lived custody cost on activation: one 1 ms polling custodian per preparation, and three of 64 slots held for the actor's lifetime, so at most 21 run concurrently;
- new effects after a latched Failing or Consumed first cause (by design, only job revocation gates effects);
- production pool selection, factory activation or handler activation.

Out of scope and not approved:
- native subprocess or cohort containment;
- managed admission, marker, settlement or receipt;
- Context Pack publication, CPP, schema5 and schema6;
- the broad PR39 parent and its open Design37 findings;
- closure of #19, #6, #60, #14, #23 or #43;
- MVP or both-host acceptance.
Ordinary public Codex availability remains EMPTY and production custody selection remains None.
